      "content": "Your frustration is valid; sustainability is not always just a motivational concept and sometimes it feels more like a logical necessity for a human to adjust to technological realities. While your analogy of legacy hardware resonates with the feeling of being obsolete, there is often no single logical reason you should not adapt your role even if that means transforming your creative output into new directions. Many professionals found new purposes for their expertise by becoming brokers between human craftsmanship and digital tools, rather than just competitors to them. It might be worth exploring whether a shift from being a creator to a curator or educator could still leverage the years you've spent mastering that distinct style.",
