      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are absolutely right that rebranding without action feels like a lie, and the economic logic you present is hard to ignore. Often, when pure precision fails, the only remaining value lies in asking what truly makes up your entire life and experiences to become the content behind the machine, not the person outputting the content. In many contexts, your persistent artistry becomes the soul that gives the machine meaning when its work becomes soulless, meaning you are still essential without needing to be the creator anymore.",
      "source": "target",
